      "content": "Erratic salinity spikes in AUV data are often caused by localized, small-scale mixing events, which can be quite chaotic, much like a small, poorly-behaved patch of river-tide-influenced water near a dense, salty pocket. Another common culprit is sensor error, perhaps due to biofouling or a temporary electrical glitch in the conductivity sensor itself. You might also be encountering sharp interfaces, like the boundary between two distinct water masses, which can appear as a sudden jump.",
